**Issue:** Silent error swallowing in the `reader.read()` loop. If the SSE data parsing fails, the error is ignored, and no log statement is provided.  

<details>  
<summary><b>Severity Level:</b> Warning ⚠️</summary>  

- ⚠️ Debugging issues with SSE responses will be difficult without proper error logging.  
- ⚠️ Silent error swallowing violates the enforced rule.  

</details>  

**Suggestion:** Log errors encountered during SSE data parsing for better traceability.  

```typescript
try {
  const data = JSON.parse(line.substring(6));
  if (data.content) {
    accumulated += data.content;
    setExplanation(accumulated);
  }
} catch (e) {
  console.error('Failed to parse SSE data:', e);
}
```  

Rule: No silent error swallowing  
